{"title":"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2025 USAMO #1</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2025 USAJMO #2</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers. Prove that there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that for every odd integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/41828839bdbce311cf0d292fa5cc636454911d09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />,  the digits in the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/7371e478d919c41803f3932047acd489c69687f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> are all greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We define a remainder operation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a5f2af3d695ba59b205a381df06b823298ee222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\,a \\bmod b\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> to be the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. \nAlso, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> be the usual floor function.\n</p><p>Base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98e656410c779472d72a475496f9fceff6dd253e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> Representation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/79418ecf275ab03231a42da3a05fc978c4c48fb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^k \\;=\\; a_{k-1}\\,(2n)^{k-1} \\;+\\; a_{k-2}\\,(2n)^{k-2} \\;+\\;\\dots\\;+\\;a_1\\,(2n)\\;+\\;a_0,\\]\" width=\"473\" height=\"20\" />\nwhere each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f43fc88c94e1f7e72cede90b3a98b31f5d4fd292.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le a_i &lt; 2n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" />  \nHence, the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98e656410c779472d72a475496f9fceff6dd253e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/7371e478d919c41803f3932047acd489c69687f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b84046052cc8b7f13b2362de2fa27bdad419e56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-1}\\,a_{k-2}\\,\\dots\\,a_1\\,a_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Leading Digit:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2cacdbe674787eac6e683b68e4a8611bd0ecb39d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{k-1}  \\;=\\;  \\left\\lfloor  \\dfrac{n^k}{(2n)^{k-1}} \\right\\rfloor \\;=\\; \\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{n}{2^{k-1}} \\right\\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>General Digit Formula:\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f019af972d6e73aa4f8f245f07dfdb68f3f8195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le i &lt; k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe3bfe3ee70842b0f93d87d221568e0e175e22d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i  \\;=\\; \\left\\lfloor  \\dfrac{\\,n^k \\bmod (2n)^{\\,i+1}}{(2n)^i} \\right\\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, one can show \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93dc192a9d2b0cc4c4f12dcab963392cd9b1cb63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^k \\bmod (2n)^{\\,i+1} \\;\\ge\\; n^{\\,i+1},\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />\nwhich implies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/27849ba410056c26ae3687e20b9b88a75e4c35cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i  \\;\\ge\\; \\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{n^{\\,i+1}}{(2n)^i} \\right\\rfloor \\;=\\; \\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{n}{2^i} \\right\\rfloor \\;\\ge\\; 2^{\\,k-1-i} \\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{n}{2^{\\,k-1}} \\right\\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> grows large, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/e/a0e1626d8e9f9253e3585bbac3d08c48aa9f08ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigl\\lfloor n / 2^{\\,k-1}\\bigr\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"75\" height=\"24\" />  \nbecomes arbitrarily big, so each digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> eventually exceeds any fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fc20cbb9094799e89db1f2762f5f073abe9d1bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />  \nHence there exists an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that for all odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/3293e8e5968cf6dba46076a1349f16af149b7255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> in the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98e656410c779472d72a475496f9fceff6dd253e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/7371e478d919c41803f3932047acd489c69687f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> are all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c70993f7967ffd6b576cce5096a37fbbd0affac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; d.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO\" title=\"2025 USAMO\">2025 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO\" title=\"2025 USAJMO\">2025 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017131921\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 245/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2458/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 205/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6285/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   36.459      1 -total\n 35.97%   13.113      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 21.11%    7.695      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 14.55%    5.306      1 Template:Duplicate\n 13.47%    4.910      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31345:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017131921 and revision id 279373. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}